. *-----------------------------------------------------
. * 2.  LOG FILE
. *-----------------------------------------------------
. * A NAMED log (ga_did) is used rather than the default one.  Stata allows
. * several named logs open at once, and a named log never collides with the
. * default log, so this works whether the script is run standalone or called
. * by Stata_code10.do -- and closing this one does not close the master's.
. *
. * Opened here, after -clear all-, so that the whole estimation sequence is
. * captured.  -clear all- does not close logs, but opening afterwards removes
. * any doubt.  Closed at the end of the script; see CLOSE-OUT below.
. * Derived from $out_root unconditionally, for the reason given in section 1.
. * NOTE the directory name is "logs", not "log" -- the singular form was the
. * stale value that misdirected RDD.log on 19 Aug 2026.
. local cur "$log_dir"

. global log_dir "$out_root/logs"

. if "`cur'" != "" & "`cur'" != "$log_dir" {
.     di as text "Georgia_DiD.do: replacing inherited log_dir (`cur')"
. }

. di as text "Georgia_DiD.do: log_dir = $log_dir"
Georgia_DiD.do: log_dir = C:/Users/marvi/Dropbox/Book/2nd Edition/Chapter 10/Output/logs

. capture mkdir "$log_dir"

